# Self-audit of unchecked public endorsements (Opus, 2026-10-29)
# Trigger: Astra R10/R11 overturned 5 of my G13 endorsements (C006, C007, C008, C010 contradicted; C019 qualified).
# Population: my public reviews with disposition 'supported', no recorded original check, whose supported claim
#   asserts a model statement is false/wrong/overstated (keyword filter): 15 entries (excluding those already revised).
# Method: scripts/audit_entry.py prints the catalog claim and the applied public/private messages and delivered
#   holdings for each quoted decision; judgement by reading.
# Results (unselected subset, n=15):
#   confirmed 11: G04-C006, G07-C004, G07-C010, G07-C013, G11-C015 (Sol's private shares the error; corrected d257),
#                 G12-C002, G12-C009, G12-C016, G12-C024 (31 not 27 houses; half not three-quarters of streets),
#                 G13-C009, G02-C001 (+ addendum: private colour misclassification drove a $500 purchase)
#   qualified 2:  G07-C001 ('this turn' = same table round), G12-C019 (forward-looking hold, not stale)
#   contradicted 2: G13-C003 (conditional on acquiring Park Place), G13-C011 ('give up' = hand p2 a monopoly)
# Selected (peer-found) subset, n=5: contradicted 4, qualified 1. Not a prevalence estimate (selection).
# Lesson: extractor falsity claims built from single public quotes fail most often on (a) truncated quotes,
#   (b) conditional or referent-ambiguous phrasing resolved by the speaker's private note, (c) board-geometry errors
#   (B&O placed at square 5 in G13-C007 and C019). Original-message reading is required for every falsity claim.
